Requirements: 24   with obligations: 23   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Requirement decomposition mis-shapes two kinds of task-file text.
    -> mis-shape-two-text-kinds  [functional/explicit]
       Handle both kinds of task-file text correctly when decomposing requirements.

[task-02] An acceptance criterion phrased "a test asserts that X" is derived into an
    obligation stating X, with the demand for a test removed. That obligation is
    indistinguishable from an obligation to implement X, so a review can report the
    behaviour delivered while the demanded test was never written.
    -> test-assertion-derives-behaviour-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       Derive an obligation stating the asserted behaviour from an acceptance criterion
       phrased as a test assertion, without carrying forward the demand for a test.
    -> behaviour-and-test-not-same-requirement  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-02, completion-03)
       Treat an obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test of
       that behaviour as distinct requirements.

[task-03] A bullet under a scope exclusions heading is dispositioned inconsistently.
    Siblings worded alike receive different treatment within a single run and different
    treatment between runs, and some are disposed of with a reason that states a
    property the change must preserve — an obligation written into a free-text field
    instead of yielded.
    -> scope-exclusion-siblings-consistent  [functional/explicit]
       Disposition sibling bullets under a scope exclusions heading consistently within
       a run and across runs, and keep free-text reasons from stating preserved
       properties.

[task-04] Make both kinds of text derive predictably.
    -> predictable-derivation-for-both-text-kinds  [functional/explicit]
       Make derivation predictable for both kinds of task-file text.

[constraint-01] An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose
    demand is the test, not the behaviour the test is about.
    -> acceptance-test-demand-is-test  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-02)
       Derive an obligation whose demand is the test itself when an acceptance criterion
       says that a test asserts something.

[constraint-02] An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test
    of that behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.
    -> behaviour-and-test-not-same-requirement  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-02, completion-03)
       Treat an obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test of
       that behaviour as distinct requirements.

[constraint-03] A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation
    regardless of which task file it appears in.
    -> same-shape-same-obligation-kind  [invariant/explicit]
       A sentence with a given shape yields the same kind of obligation regardless of
       which task file it appears in.

[constraint-04] Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
    disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-exclusions-same-disposition  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       Apply the same disposition to sibling bullets worded alike under one scope
       exclusions heading.

[constraint-05] A requirement disposed of without an obligation carries a reason that
    does not itself state a property the change must preserve.
    -> no-preserve-property-reason  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       Use a reason for no-obligation dispositions that does not state a property the
       change must preserve.

[constraint-06] No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test
    that an excluded thing did not happen.
    -> no-obligation-for-excluded-thing-not-happening  [invariant/explicit]
       No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test that an
       excluded thing did not happen.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-task-text-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Produce byte-identical review state for two runs over byte-identical task text.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-issue-no-live-model-calls  [invariant/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> scope-of-test-evidence-outside-this-change  [human_review/explicit]
       Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all remains outside the scope of
       this change.

[exclusion-02] Assigning obligation types, which is #205.
    -> obligation-types-assigned-separately  [human_review/explicit]
       Assigning obligation types remains a separate concern from this change.

[exclusion-03] Which open questions are raised, and what they cite, which is #206.
    -> open-questions-and-citations  [human_review/explicit]
       Raise open questions only for materially underspecified requirements, and include
       what each question cites.

[exclusion-04] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> requirement-splitting-granularity  [invariant/explicit]
       Split a single requirement into obligations at the level of distinct computations
       while keeping cohesive behaviors whole.

[exclusion-05] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> stable-obligation-identifiers  [compatibility/explicit]
       Keep obligation identifiers stable across task-file edits.

[exclusion-06] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> decomposition-accuracy-measurement  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Measure how accurate the decomposition is.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       A standalone section label with no actionable requirement.

